==============================================================================
PHASE 2: DO NOT APPLY OR DEPLOY WITHOUT USER APPROVAL
==============================================================================
Migration: PRD-SCHEMA-P1 (production order & output reporting module)
Repo destination: scripts/migrations/production-schema-p1/phase2/google-apps-script.phase2.patch

What it changes (2 files; nothing else):
  scripts/google-apps-script.gs
    - ALLOWED_ACTIONS += 'productionCommand'
    - validatePayload: productionCommand skips the generic sheetName check and
      runs validateProductionCommand() (own allowlist PRD_CMD_SHEETS; ProductionCounters
      is reachable ONLY through this command, it is NOT added to ALLOWED_SHEETS)
    - PRODUCTION_SHEET_HEADERS: appends the PRD-SCHEMA-P1 columns so an auto-created
      production tab matches the migration
    - inlines phase2/production-command.gs verbatim (single-file Apps Script deployment)
    - doPost: routes productionCommand inside the existing script lock
  src/server/google-sheets/script-signer.ts
    - ALLOWED_ACTIONS += "productionCommand"; payload shape checks;
      refuses productionCommand in GOOGLE_SCRIPT_LEGACY_MODE (unsigned requests)
Not changed: append/update/deleteRow/atomicStockOperation behave exactly as today, so the
current app keeps working before its production code is switched to productionCommand.

Base: branch refactor/structure @ 15f92ff
  scripts/google-apps-script.gs              sha256 f197cdf7dff19e79185c0369c95ef29510aead9679a1ca39b0ea1d30be8cb519
  src/server/google-sheets/script-signer.ts  sha256 eb9c97eaa17b7911c7b573d860e3a8fc1bf174e95e5d62ec51bd8967387b887a

Preconditions (ALL required, in order):
  1. Explicit user approval to change and redeploy the LIVE Apps Script web app.
  2. Migration PRD-SCHEMA-P1 applied + verified on the target sheet (copy first, then live
     with its own approval). doProductionCommand fails closed if column AB does not exist.
  3. Backend Dev's production service switched to productionCommand (CAS on version +
     updated_at) and deployed together with this; never deploy one without the other.
  4. Rehearsal on the sheet COPY with its own web-app deployment + its own signing secret.

Check / apply (from the repo root, only after approval):
  git apply --check scripts/migrations/production-schema-p1/phase2/google-apps-script.phase2.patch
  git apply         scripts/migrations/production-schema-p1/phase2/google-apps-script.phase2.patch
  # Then paste scripts/google-apps-script.gs into the Apps Script editor and
  # Deploy -> Manage deployments -> Edit -> New version (keeps the same /exec URL).
Rollback: Manage deployments -> Edit -> select the previous version; `git apply -R` the patch.
Offline tests: node scripts/migrations/production-schema-p1/phase2/test/run-phase2-tests.js
  (add PATCHED_GS=scripts/google-apps-script.gs after applying, to test the routed path)
